<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm8a-wenchang ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 8A (unknown payload, Wenchang Commercial LC-1) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
thrust SL/vac interpolated on ambient pressure, mdot from Isp, staging/fairing/coast events; vertical rise to 17.0 s (rule: config guidance),
pitch kick 4.815 deg over 10 s, gravity turn, linear-tangent upper-stage steering tan(theta)=0.5782-0.001439*(t-t_ign), solved by optimizer.
Vehicle config: Long March 8A (sim/vehicles/lm8a.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
LM-8A: thrusts/Isp/GLOW from Wikipedia; stage masses DERIVED from LM-8 vs core-only GLOW differences plus ASSUMED propellant fractions.
FLOWN 2026-10-25T02:03Z (Sat Oct 24 7:03 pm PDT), success, per Xinhua/LL2: utc_iso shifted +13 min from the planned 01:50Z T0; geometry is the pre-flight ILLUSTRATIVE profile, unchanged. Pre-flight: LL2 NET 01:50Z, orbit Unknown.
Target (see launch config): insertion 700 km, apoapsis 700 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 140.40 deg; payload 5000 kg.
Pad: 19.597275N 110.930753E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-25T02:03:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (CASC/CALT did not publish a payload-separation time; payload and orbit unannounced). From insertion T+763.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 98.87 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast.
POST-CUTOFF end T+12627 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 700.03 km, osculating 700.0 x 709.1 km, i 54.111 deg.</description>
